# Releasing Cozip.jl

Cozip.jl uses libcozip binaries from the GitHub release. Register the Julia package only after the release workflow adds the new `julia/Artifacts.toml` to `main`.

## Steps

1. Set the root `VERSION` to today's CalVer value, run `make sync` and complete the local tests.
2. Commit the release, tag that commit `v<version>` and push `main`. After the pre-release checks pass, push that tag. The tag starts `release.yml`.
3. Wait for every release job, including `regenerate-artifacts-toml`, to pass. That last job pushes an `Artifacts.toml` commit to `main`.
4. Fetch that commit and update the local checkout:

   ```bash
   git fetch origin main
   git merge --ff-only origin/main
   ```

5. Register the Julia package from the repo root:

   ```bash
   julia -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.Registry.update("AsteriskRegistry"); using LocalRegistry; register("./julia"; registry="AsteriskRegistry", push=true)'
   ```

The registry must point to the commit containing the new `Artifacts.toml`; registering the tagged commit would keep the previous release's binaries.

## Verify

In a fresh Julia environment, install the registered package and check the loaded library version:

```julia
using Pkg
Pkg.activate(; temp=true)
Pkg.Registry.add(Pkg.RegistrySpec(url="https://github.com/asterisk-labs/AsteriskRegistry"))
Pkg.add("Cozip")
using Cozip
Cozip.LibCozip.cozip_version()
```

The result should equal `VERSION`. If the registry already exists in the Julia depot, update it instead of adding it again.
